# 🚀 E-Commerce Microservices

## My Personal Project Handbook

> Ye file mere liye hai — jab bhi mujhe project ka flow, technology, ports, Docker, Redis, Nginx ya deployment bhool jaye, is file ko ek baar read karunga.

---

# 1. 🧠 Project ka Main Idea

Hum ek **Basic E-Commerce Microservices Platform** bana rahe hain.

Is project mein main backend ko ek single application ki jagah multiple independent services mein divide kar raha hoon.

### Main Services

```text
Product Service
      ↓
Products ka kaam

Order Service
      ↓
Orders + Users + Authentication ka kaam
```

Frontend directly services se baat nahi karega.

Frontend → Nginx → Proper Service

---

# 2. 🏗️ Complete Architecture

```text
                         👤 CUSTOMER
                              │
                              ▼
                       ⚛️ REACT FRONTEND
                              │
                              ▼
                     🌐 NGINX GATEWAY
                        API GATEWAY
                              │
                 ┌────────────┴────────────┐
                 │                         │
                 ▼                         ▼
        📦 PRODUCT SERVICE          🛒 ORDER SERVICE
             :4001                      :4002
                 │                         │
          ┌──────┴──────┐            ┌─────┴─────┐
          │             │            │           │
          ▼             ▼            ▼           ▼
       Neon DB       Redis        Neon DB      Redis
          │                          │
          ▼                          ▼
      Products                    Orders
```

---

# 3. 🧩 Technologies We Are Using

| Technology     | Main Work                             |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Node.js        | JavaScript runtime                    |
| Express        | Backend API framework                 |
| PostgreSQL     | Permanent database                    |
| Neon           | Cloud PostgreSQL                      |
| Prisma         | Database ORM                          |
| Redis          | Cache + Pub/Sub                       |
| Upstash Redis  | Cloud Redis                           |
| Axios          | Service-to-service HTTP communication |
| JWT            | Authentication                        |
| bcrypt         | Password hashing                      |
| Nodemailer     | Email sending                         |
| Nginx          | API Gateway                           |
| Docker         | Application containerization          |
| Docker Compose | Multiple containers manage/run        |
| Git/GitHub     | Source code management                |
| AWS EC2        | Cloud server                          |
| Ubuntu         | EC2 operating system                  |
| React/Vite     | Frontend                              |

---

# 4. 🏠 Database Per Service

Humne microservices mein databases ko separate rakha hai.

```text
Product Service
      │
      ▼
ecommerce-product-db
      │
      ▼
Neon PostgreSQL
```

Aur:

```text
Order Service
      │
      ▼
ecommerce-order-db
      │
      ▼
Neon PostgreSQL
```

### Important

Product Service directly Order DB ko access nahi karta.

Order Service directly Product DB ko access nahi karta.

Har service apne database ki responsibility rakhti hai.

---

# 5. 📦 Product Service

Product Service ka kaam:

```text
Create Product
Get Products
Get Product By ID
Update Product
Delete Product
Reduce Stock
```

### Product Port

```text
4001
```

### Product APIs

```text
POST    /api/products
GET     /api/products
GET     /api/products/:id
PUT     /api/products/:id
DELETE  /api/products/:id
```

---

# 6. 🛒 Order Service

Order Service ka kaam:

```text
Users
Authentication
Orders
Order status
Forgot password
OTP
Email
```

### Order Port

```text
4002
```

### Order APIs

```text
POST    /api/orders
GET     /api/orders
GET     /api/orders/:id
PUT     /api/orders/:id
DELETE  /api/orders/:id
```

Authentication:

```text
/api/auth/...
```

---

# 7. 🔐 Authentication Flow

User login karta hai:

```text
User
 │
 ▼
POST /api/auth/login
 │
 ▼
Order Service :4002
 │
 ▼
Find User in PostgreSQL
 │
 ▼
bcrypt password verify
 │
 ▼
JWT generate
 │
 ▼
JWT cookie mein store
 │
 ▼
User authenticated
```

Protected API:

```text
Request
  │
  ▼
JWT Cookie
  │
  ▼
authenticateUser middleware
  │
  ▼
JWT verify
  │
  ▼
req.user
  │
  ▼
Controller
```

---

# 8. 👑 Role Based Authorization

User ke role ke basis par access control hota hai.

Example:

```text
user
admin
```

Admin-only API:

```text
Request
   ↓
authenticateUser
   ↓
authorizeRoles("admin")
   ↓
Admin allowed?
   ↓
YES → Controller
NO  → 403
```

### Important

Authentication = **Who are you?**

Authorization = **What are you allowed to do?**

---

# 9. 🔑 Forgot Password Flow

```text
User email deta hai
        ↓
User exists?
   ↓           ↓
 NO           YES
 ↓              ↓
Error       Generate OTP
               ↓
          Save OTP in DB
               ↓
          Send OTP Email
               ↓
          User receives OTP
               ↓
           Verify OTP
               ↓
       OTP correct + valid?
               ↓
              YES
               ↓
           Delete OTP
               ↓
         New Password
               ↓
         bcrypt.hash()
               ↓
        Update User DB
               ↓
       Password Changed ✅
```

### OTP

```text
OTP expiry = 2 minutes
```

Reset JWT:

```text
10 minutes
```

---

# 10. ⚡ Redis

Redis ko humne **2 different purposes** ke liye use kiya hai.

```text
Redis
 │
 ├── Cache
 │
 └── Pub/Sub
```

---

# 11. 🧠 Redis Cache

### Definition

**Caching is the process of storing frequently accessed data in a fast temporary storage so that future requests can be served faster.**

Simple:

Database se baar-baar same data lene ke bajaye Redis mein temporary copy rakh dete hain.

---

## Product Cache

```text
GET /api/products
       ↓
Product Service
       ↓
Redis mein products hai?
    ↓          ↓
   YES         NO
    ↓           ↓
Return       PostgreSQL
              ↓
           Redis mein save
              ↓
           Return data
```

Cache key:

```text
products
```

Expiry:

```text
60 seconds
```

---

## Individual Product Cache

```text
GET /api/products/prod-001
          ↓
Redis
          ↓
product:prod-001
```

Agar Redis mein nahi:

```text
Redis miss
   ↓
PostgreSQL
   ↓
Redis
   ↓
Response
```

---

# 12. 🗑️ Cache Invalidation

Agar product change ho gaya to purana Redis data galat ho sakta hai.

Isliye:

```text
CREATE PRODUCT
     ↓
DB update
     ↓
Delete "products" cache
```

Update:

```text
UPDATE PRODUCT
     ↓
DB update
     ↓
Delete product:id
     ↓
Delete products
```

Delete:

```text
DELETE PRODUCT
     ↓
DB delete
     ↓
Delete product:id
     ↓
Delete products
```

### Important concept

**Cache invalidation = removing/updating stale cached data when the original data changes.**

---

# 13. 📢 Redis Pub/Sub

### Definition

**Publish/Subscribe is a messaging pattern where a publisher sends an event to a channel and subscribers interested in that channel receive the event.**

Simple language:

Ek service bolti hai:

> "Order create ho gaya."

Aur jis service ko is event mein interest hai, wo sun leti hai.

---

# 14. 📢 Pub/Sub Architecture

```text
                  ORDER SERVICE
                       │
                       │
                       │ order.created
                       ▼
                ┌───────────────┐
                │ Redis Pub/Sub │
                └───────┬───────┘
                        │
              ┌─────────┴──────────┐
              │                    │
              ▼                    ▼
      Product Subscriber      Email Subscriber
              │                    │
              ▼                    ▼
        Reduce Stock          Send Email
```

Channel:

```text
order.created
```

---

# 15. 🛒 Complete POST Order Flow

Ye project ka one of the most important flows hai.

```text
Postman / React
      │
      │ POST /api/orders
      ▼
localhost:8080
      │
      ▼
    NGINX
      │
      ▼
Order Service :4002
      │
      ├──────────────► Product Service :4001
      │                    │
      │                    ▼
      │               Check Product
      │               Check Price
      │               Check Stock
      │
      ▼
Save Order
      │
      ▼
Order PostgreSQL
      │
      ▼
Publish "order.created"
      │
      ▼
Redis Pub/Sub
      │
      ├───────────────────┐
      │                   │
      ▼                   ▼
Product Service       Email Handler
      │                   │
      ▼                   ▼
Reduce Stock          Send Email
      │
      ▼
Product DB
```

---

# 16. 🔄 HTTP vs Pub/Sub

Ye difference yaad rakhna important hai.

| Technology    | Meaning                     |
| ------------- | --------------------------- |
| HTTP/Axios    | Direct request/response     |
| Redis Cache   | Fast temporary data         |
| Redis Pub/Sub | Event/message communication |
| PostgreSQL    | Permanent data              |

### Example HTTP

```text
Order Service
     │
     │ GET product
     ▼
Product Service
     │
     ▼
Response
```

Order Service ko answer chahiye.

---

### Example Pub/Sub

```text
Order Service
     │
     │ "Order created!"
     ▼
Redis
     │
     ├──► Product Service
     │
     └──► Email Handler
```

Yahan Order Service ko har subscriber ka direct response nahi chahiye.

---

# 17. 🔌 Ports — Sabse Important

Project mein ports ko lekar confusion ho sakta hai.

### Services

```text
Product Service = 4001
Order Service   = 4002
```

Lekin client normally in ports ko use nahi karta.

Local mein:

```text
Client
  ↓
localhost:8080
  ↓
Nginx
  ↓
4001 / 4002
```

---

# 18. 🌐 Local Port Flow

```text
Postman / Browser / React
          │
          ▼
localhost:8080
          │
          ▼
      Nginx :80
          │
     ┌────┴────┐
     │         │
     ▼         ▼
   :4001     :4002
 Product      Order
```

### `8080:80` ka meaning

```text
8080 = Host machine port
80   = Nginx container port
```

Docker Compose:

```yaml
ports:
  - "8080:80"
```

Matlab:

```text
Windows localhost:8080
          ↓
Docker Nginx :80
```

---

# 19. 🧠 4001 / 4002 Ka Actual Meaning

```text
4001 → Product Service container ke andar application
4002 → Order Service container ke andar application
```

Ye ports service ko identify karne ke liye hain.

Nginx:

```text
/api/products
      ↓
product-service:4001
```

```text
/api/orders
      ↓
order-service:4002
```

---

# 20. 🐳 Docker

### Definition

**Docker is a platform used to package an application with its dependencies and run it consistently inside containers.**

Simple:

Mera application + dependencies + required environment ko ek package jaisa bana deta hai.

---

# 21. 🖼️ Docker Image

### Definition

**An image is a packaged blueprint used to create containers.**

Example:

```text
Dockerfile
    ↓
docker build
    ↓
Docker Image
```

---

# 22. 📦 Docker Container

### Definition

**A container is a running instance of a Docker image.**

```text
Image
  ↓
docker run
  ↓
Container
```

Ek image se multiple containers bhi ban sakte hain.

---

# 23. 📝 Dockerfile

### Definition

**A Dockerfile contains instructions used to build a Docker image.**

Product Service Dockerfile:

```dockerfile
FROM node:22

WORKDIR /app

COPY package*.json ./

RUN npm install

COPY . .

RUN npx prisma generate

EXPOSE 4001

CMD ["npm", "start"]
```

### Iska flow

```text
FROM node:22
      ↓
Node environment

WORKDIR /app
      ↓
Container ke andar working folder

COPY package*.json ./
      ↓
Package files copy

RUN npm install
      ↓
Dependencies install

COPY . .
      ↓
Project code copy

RUN npx prisma generate
      ↓
Prisma Client generate

EXPOSE 4001
      ↓
Application ka container port

CMD npm start
      ↓
Application start
```

---

# 24. 📄 .dockerignore

```text
node_modules
.env
.git
npm-debug.log
```

### Why?

`node_modules`:

```text
Local wala copy nahi karna
```

Docker image ke andar:

```text
npm install
```

se dependencies dobara install hongi.

`.env`:

```text
Secrets image mein nahi daalne.
```

---

# 25. 🔐 Environment Variables

### Definition

**Environment variables store configuration and sensitive values outside the source code.**

Example:

```env
DATABASE_URL="..."
REDIS_URL="..."
JWT_SECRET="..."
EMAIL_USER="..."
EMAIL_PASS="..."
```

GitHub mein `.env` nahi.

Docker image mein `.env` nahi.

Runtime par environment variables inject karte hain.

---

# 26. 🌐 Docker Network

Docker Compose automatically services ko ek network mein connect karta hai.

Isliye containers ek dusre ko service name se access kar sakte hain.

Example:

```text
Order Service
     │
     │ HTTP
     ▼
http://product-service:4001
```

Yahan:

```text
product-service
```

container/service ka naam hai.

---

# 27. ❌ Container ke andar localhost

Ye important mistake hai:

```text
http://localhost:4001
```

Order container se use karoge to iska matlab hoga:

```text
Order Service ka khud ka localhost
```

Product Service nahi.

Correct:

```text
http://product-service:4001
```

---

# 28. 🧩 Docker Compose

### Definition

**Docker Compose is a tool used to define and manage multiple containers as one application.**

Humare project mein:

```text
docker-compose.yml
        │
        ├── Product Service
        ├── Order Service
        └── Nginx
```

---

# 29. 🐳 Our Docker Compose Architecture

```text
                    Docker Compose
                          │
             ┌────────────┼────────────┐
             │            │            │
             ▼            ▼            ▼
       Product Service Order Service  Nginx
           :4001          :4002        :80
             │            │             ▲
             │            │             │
             └────────────┴─────────────┘
                       Docker Network
```

Local machine:

```text
localhost:8080
      ↓
Nginx container :80
```

Compose mapping:

```yaml
ports:
  - "8080:80"
```

---

# 30. 🌐 API Gateway

### Definition

**An API Gateway is a centralized entry point through which clients access backend services.**

Humne API Gateway ka kaam Nginx se karwaya.

Important:

```text
API Gateway = Role / Concept

Nginx = Software
```

Nginx API Gateway ka role perform kar raha hai.

---

# 31. ⚙️ Nginx

Nginx ka kaam:

```text
Client request
      ↓
Nginx
      ↓
URL dekho
      ↓
Correct Service ko request bhejo
```

### nginx.conf

```nginx
location /api/products {
    proxy_pass http://product-service:4001;
}

location /api/orders {
    proxy_pass http://order-service:4002;
}

location /api/auth {
    proxy_pass http://order-service:4002;
}
```

---

# 32. 🚦 Nginx Routing

Products:

```text
localhost:8080/api/products
             ↓
          Nginx :80
             ↓
product-service:4001
```

Orders:

```text
localhost:8080/api/orders
             ↓
          Nginx :80
             ↓
order-service:4002
```

Auth:

```text
localhost:8080/api/auth/login
             ↓
          Nginx :80
             ↓
order-service:4002
```

---

# 33. 🧠 Client ko kya pata hai?

Client ko internally ye pata hona zaroori nahi:

```text
4001
4002
product-service
order-service
```

Client simply:

```text
localhost:8080
```

use karta hai.

```text
Client
  │
  │ Only knows
  ▼
localhost:8080
  │
  ▼
Nginx
  │
  ├── /api/products → Product :4001
  │
  └── /api/orders   → Order :4002
```

---

# 34. 🧪 Postman ka Game

### GET Products

```text
GET
http://localhost:8080/api/products
```

Flow:

```text
Postman
  ↓
8080
  ↓
Nginx
  ↓
Product :4001
  ↓
Redis / DB
  ↓
Response
  ↓
Postman
```

---

### POST Product

```text
POST
http://localhost:8080/api/products
```

Flow:

```text
Postman
  ↓
8080
  ↓
Nginx
  ↓
Product :4001
  ↓
PostgreSQL
  ↓
Delete products cache
  ↓
Response
```

---

### POST Order

```text
POST
http://localhost:8080/api/orders
```

Flow:

```text
Postman
  ↓
8080
  ↓
Nginx
  ↓
Order :4002
  ↓
Product Service :4001
  ↓
Check Product
  ↓
Order DB
  ↓
order.created
  ↓
Redis Pub/Sub
  ├── Product → Reduce Stock
  └── Email → Send Confirmation
```

---

# 35. 📡 API Gateway ke baad Ports

### Local

```text
Client
  ↓
localhost:8080
  ↓
Nginx :80
  ↓
4001 / 4002
```

### EC2

```text
Internet
  ↓
EC2 Public IP :80
  ↓
Nginx :80
  ↓
4001 / 4002
```

### Remember

```text
LOCAL:
localhost:8080 → Nginx → 4001 / 4002

EC2:
Public-IP:80 → Nginx → 4001 / 4002
```

