# 36. 🐳 Docker Commands I Learned

## Build Image

```bash
docker build -t product-service .
```

Meaning:

```text
Dockerfile
   ↓
Build
   ↓
product-service image
```

---

## See Images

```bash
docker images
```

---

## Run Container

```bash
docker run --env-file .env -p 4001:4001 product-service
```

### Port mapping

```text
-p HOST:CONTAINER
```

Example:

```text
-p 4001:4001
```

---

## See Running Containers

```bash
docker ps
```

---

## See All Containers

```bash
docker ps -a
```

---

## Stop Container

```bash
docker stop <container_id>
```

---

## Start Container

```bash
docker start <container_name>
```

---

## Remove Container

```bash
docker rm <container_name>
```

---

## Remove Unused Containers

```bash
docker container prune
```

---

## Clean Unused Docker Resources

```bash
docker system prune -a
```

Careful: ye unused Docker resources remove kar sakta hai.

---

# 37. 🐳 Docker Compose Commands

Project root:

```text
ecommerce-microservices/
```

### Start

```bash
docker-compose up
```

### Background mein start

```bash
docker-compose up -d
```

### Build + Start

```bash
docker-compose up --build -d
```

### Stop/remove Compose resources

```bash
docker-compose down
```

### Check containers

```bash
docker-compose ps
```

### Logs

```bash
docker-compose logs
```

Specific service:

```bash
docker-compose logs product-service
```

