# 53. 🧠 Technologies Ka Simple Cheat Sheet

```text
Node.js
→ JavaScript backend run karta hai

Express
→ APIs/server banane ke liye

PostgreSQL
→ Permanent data

Neon
→ Cloud PostgreSQL

Prisma
→ Database ke saath easy interaction

Redis
→ Fast cache + Pub/Sub

Upstash
→ Cloud Redis

Axios
→ Service-to-service HTTP request

JWT
→ Authentication

bcrypt
→ Password hashing

Nodemailer
→ Email send

Nginx
→ API Gateway / reverse proxy

Docker
→ Application package/run

Dockerfile
→ Image ka blueprint/instructions

Docker Image
→ Packaged application blueprint

Container
→ Running image

Docker Compose
→ Multiple containers manage/connect

Docker Network
→ Containers ko communicate karata hai

.env
→ Runtime configuration/secrets

AWS EC2
→ Cloud server

Ubuntu
→ Server operating system

SSH
→ Secure remote server connection
```

---

# 54. 🔌 Ports Cheat Sheet

```text
4001
↓
Product Service

4002
↓
Order Service

80
↓
Nginx container port

8080
↓
Local host port
```

### Local

```text
localhost:8080
       ↓
    Nginx :80
       ↓
  4001 / 4002
```

### EC2

```text
PUBLIC_IP:80
       ↓
    Nginx :80
       ↓
  4001 / 4002
```

---

# 55. 🧠 Most Important Things To Remember

### 1.

```text
4001 = Product
4002 = Order
```

### 2.

```text
8080 = Local Nginx entry point
```

### 3.

```text
Nginx decides where request goes.
```

### 4.

```text
Docker service name is used for
container-to-container communication.
```

Example:

```text
http://product-service:4001
```

### 5.

```text
Redis Cache = data fast access ke liye
```

### 6.

```text
Redis Pub/Sub = event/message communication
```

### 7.

```text
HTTP/Axios = direct communication
```

### 8.

```text
PostgreSQL = permanent data
```

### 9.

```text
Dockerfile = image kaise banegi
```

### 10.

```text
docker-compose.yml = containers kaise run/connect honge
```

### 11.

```text
API Gateway = concept/role
Nginx = software
```

### 12.

```text
Client → Nginx → Service
```

